codex
I’m about to rewrite `codex_scientific_text.md` with a bash-built extraction: keep the current YAML/header block, append a cleaned body from `revised2.tex`, and normalize the most common LaTeX inline commands so the scientific text reads as plain markdown.
codex
The extraction pass is ready. I’m applying it now, then I’ll inspect the markdown for leftover TeX scaffolding and patch any small issues by hand.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc 'tmpfile=$(mktemp /private/tmp/qft_extract.XXXXXX.md)
{
  sed -n '"'1,/"'^# Scientific TeX Extract$/p'"' codex_scientific_text.md
  printf '\\n'
  perl -0pe '
    s/.*?\\\\begin\\{document\\}\\s*//s;
    s/\\\\begin\\{thebibliography\\}.*?\\\\end\\{thebibliography\\}//sg;
    s/\\\\end\\{document\\}.*//s;
    s/(?<"'!'"\\\\)%.*"'$//mg;
    s/'"\\\\title\\{(.*?)\\}\\s*/do { my "'$t = $1; $t =~ s/'"\\s+/ /g; \"## "'$t'"\\\\n\\\\n\" }/seg;
    s/\\\\author\\{.*?\\}\\s*//sg;
    s/\\\\affiliation\\{.*?\\}\\s*//sg;
    s/\\\\pacs\\{.*?\\}\\s*//sg;
    s/\\\\maketitle\\s*//g;
    s/\\\\begin\\{abstract\\}\\s*/**Abstract.** /g;
    s/\\s*\\\\end\\{abstract\\}\\s*/\\\\n\\\\n/g;
    s/\\\\begin\\{figure\\*?\\}.*?\\\\end\\{figure\\*?\\}\\s*//sg;
    s/\\\\begin\\{equation\\}/\\\\n"'$$'"\\\\n/g;
    s/\\\\end\\{equation\\}/\\\\n"'$$'"\\\\n/g;
    s/\\\\label\\{["'^}]+'"\\}//g;
    s/\\\\onlinecite\\{(["'^}]*)'"\\}/[Ref: "'$1]/g;
    s/'"\\\\cite\\{(["'^}]*)'"\\}/[Refs: "'$1]/g;
    s/'"\\\\eqref\\{(["'^}]*)'"\\}/("'$1)/g;
    s/'"\\\\ref\\{(["'^}]*)'"\\}/"'$1/g;
    s/'"\\{\\\\it\\s+(["'^}]*)'"\\}/*"'$1*/g;
    s/'"\\\\emph\\{(["'^}]*)'"\\}/*"'$1*/g;
    s/We thank Sankar das Sarma and Steve Simon for'"\\s+helpful discussions\\.\\s+This work was supported by NSF grant\\s+DMR-0605066, and by ACS PRF grant 44776-AC10\\.\\s*//s;
    s/[ \\t]+\\n/\\n/g;
    s/\\n{3,}/\\n\\n/g;
    s/"'^'"\\s+//;
    s/\\s+"'$//;
  '"' revised2.tex
} > \""'$tmpfile"
